Zork I: The Great Underground Empire, for z3

zork1.z3 is Infocom's final release of Zork I (release 119, serial
880429, 86838 bytes), a version 3 Z-machine story file.  It is
COMPILED/zork1.z3 from Microsoft's https://github.com/historicalsource/zork1
at commit 97b7b3d (2025-11-21), which Microsoft released under the MIT
licence in LICENSE beside it.  The licence travels with the game: the
card installs both, as /usr/games/lib/zork1.z3 and
/usr/games/lib/zork1.LICENSE.

zork1.c is the command that plays it: it runs /usr/games/z3 on the
story, passing z3's options through.  It is a program because a shell
script cannot be run by name on this machine (exec hands it to bcrun,
"not a bytecode object"), and because V7 sh turns an empty "$@" into
one empty argument, which z3 took for the story file.

The game reports itself as "Release 2" under z3: fweep writes 0x0802
over the release number in the header (version_init), which every game
it plays shows.  The story file itself is unchanged.
